        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Factoring integers in Perl, thirteen years later]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Dana has made Math::Prime::Util::GMP 0.55 publicly available. In this new version, an updated, and speedier implementation of Self-Initialising Quadratic Sieve (SIQS) for factorisation has been added. The enhancements were inspired by Hugo van der Sanden's research and have been aided by the work of coding AIs. This new feature has made factorisation faster and simpler to perform on large numbers, thereby improving memory consumption as well as the usability of the standard factor() calls by introducing msiqs, a separate multi-threaded factoring program that uses C and GMP and can successfully compete against established programs such as YAFU.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.11.06</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://blogs.perl.org/users/dana_jacobsen/2026/11/factoring-integers-in-perl-thirteen-years-later.html</guid>
            <link>https://blogs.perl.org/users/dana_jacobsen/2026/11/factoring-integers-in-perl-thirteen-years-later.html</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[dana_jacobsen]]></author>
            
                
            
            
        </item>
        
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[XS coverage for Perl]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Robert has introduced the new tool called Devel::XSCover that aims at overcoming the problem of observing the code coverage of Perl programs based on the C/XS programming languages. Unlike Devel::Cover (which only provides details about the Perl code and limited information about C through gcov), Devel::XSCover can deal with compilation options, ensure that the program works in a multithreaded environment, return the name of the Perl function linked to the C function, and provide detailed reports in HTML.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.11.03</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://lnation.org/blog/xs-coverage-for-perl-introducing-devel-xscover</guid>
            <link>https://lnation.org/blog/xs-coverage-for-perl-introducing-devel-xscover</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[robert_acock]]></author>
            
                
            
            
        </item>
        
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[NetAddr::IP 4.080_08: another trial, please smoke test]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Dean has put out a trial version known as NetAddr::IP version number 4.080_08 to CPAN intending to find out the last bugs before making this version finally stable. The new version comes with better parsing, stricter input validation apart from introducing new constructors such as new4() and NetAddr::IP::Count. Moreover, this version is being published under the MIT license.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.11.07</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://blogs.perl.org/users/dean/2026/11/netaddrip-4080-08-another-trial-please-smoke-test.html</guid>
            <link>https://blogs.perl.org/users/dean/2026/11/netaddrip-4080-08-another-trial-please-smoke-test.html</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[dean_hamstead]]></author>
            
                
            
            
